{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Give ear, O heavens.</b> For I warn Israel through them, and you shall be witnesses in the matter — for thus I said to them, that you shall be witnesses. And likewise <b>and let the earth hear.</b> And why did he call heaven and earth as witnesses? Moses said: I am flesh and blood; tomorrow I die. If Israel say, 'We did not accept the covenant upon ourselves' — who comes and refutes them? Therefore he called heaven and earth as witnesses — witnesses that endure forever. And furthermore: if they merit, the witnesses come and give their reward — the vine gives its fruit, the earth gives its produce, and the heavens give their dew. And if they incur guilt, the witnesses' hand is upon them first — ״וְעָצַר אֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְלֹא יִהְיֶה מָטָר וְהָאֲדָמָה לֹא תִתֵּן אֶת יְבוּלָהּ״ (Deuteronomy [28:23]), and afterward ״וַאֲבַדְתֶּם מְהֵרָה״ ([Deuteronomy 11:17]) at the hands of the nations."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:08.123858156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}